libprisma development commit 23b0d70 (checked out at submodules/libprisma):
bound the grammar recursion in SyntaxHighlighter::tokenize()/matchGrammar()
with a depth counter. Prism grammars generated from grammars.dat can contain
token cycles (brightscript's directive-statement <-> expression), which drove
the mutual recursion between tokenize() and matchGrammar() until the thread
stack was exhausted and the highlighter crashed with SIGSEGV. Matching now
starts at depth 0, increments only when entering an `inside` grammar, passes
the depth unchanged through greedy rematches, and stops recursing past
kMaxTokenizeDepth = 128, keeping the deepest match as plain text. The
exception handler around permitted matching is kept. Ported from the iOS
libprisma sources at submodules/telegram-ios/third-party/libprisma.

